        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(openai): add timeout to realtime client-secret requests",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenAI Realtime client-secret creation could wait indefinitely when the client-secret endpoint accepted the POST but never returned a response.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe Realtime voice and transcription secret paths share `createOpenAIRealtimeSecret`, so the timeout is applied once at the existing `fetchWithSsrFGuard` boundary. The change preserves the current SSRF allowlist, request body shape, auth headers, bounded response parsing, and 401 remediation behavior.\n\n## User Impact\n\nA stalled OpenAI-compatible client-secret endpoint no longer blocks Realtime session setup forever. Callers receive a bounded timeout-class rejection and can surface the existing setup failure path.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run extensions/openai/realtime-provider-shared.test.ts` - passed; `Test Files  1 passed (1)`, `Tests  6 passed (6)`.\n- `pnpm exec oxfmt --check --threads=1 extensions/openai/realtime-provider-shared.ts extensions/openai/realtime-provider-shared.test.ts` - passed.\n- `./node_modules/.bin/oxlint --config .oxlintrc.json --tsconfig config/tsconfig/oxlint.extensions.json extensions/openai/realtime-provider-shared.ts extensions/openai/realtime-provider-shared.test.ts` - passed; exit 0.\n- `git diff --check upstream/main..HEAD` - passed; exit 0.\n- Open PR collision check: searched open PR topics and scanned the latest 500 open PR changed-file lists; no open PR touched `extensions/openai/realtime-provider-shared.ts`.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nBehavior addressed: OpenAI Realtime client-secret POSTs now carry a deadline when the remote endpoint accepts the request but never sends a response.\n\nReal environment tested: local Linux Node source checkout; real `node:http` loopback server that accepts POSTs and deliberately never responds.\n\nExact command run after this patch: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run extensions/openai/realtime-provider-shared.test.ts`\n\nEvidence after fix: the focused regression first verifies a bare POST to the same hanging server remains pending without a deadline. It then imports the real `fetchWithSsrFGuard` runtime with `vi.importActual` and proves a real guarded POST to `/guarded` rejects with a timeout-class error. Finally, the exported `createOpenAIRealtimeClientSecret` path is exercised with a narrow test shim that only rewrites the fixed OpenAI URL to the loopback server and delegates to the real `fetchWithSsrFGuard`; this proves the helper sends `timeoutMs: 20000` at the real guarded-fetch boundary instead of relying on a hand-simulated timeout.\n\nWhat was not tested: live OpenAI traffic; the hang is reproduced with a real local HTTP server, not the real third-party service.",
